# Published repo = the app's runtime files only (owner decision 2026-09-14):
# Orga-naes.html, sw.js, manifest.json, icons, README, LICENSE, git config.
# Everything below is local development tooling and never travels.
/src/
/scripts/
/tests/
/build.mjs
/package.json
/.github/
/database.rules.json
# Firebase CLI deploy config for those rules (same local-only decision):
# firebase.json points the CLI at database.rules.json, .firebaserc maps the
# aliases, so publishing the rules is one command per project instead of a
# console paste. Both are mirrored into snapshots with the rest of the tooling.
/firebase.json
/.firebaserc
# Firebase CLI run artifacts: firebase-debug.log lands in the working directory
# on any --debug run (scripts/publish-rules.cjs removes its own on every exit path).
# This only keeps the git status output clean — backup.ps1 mirrors ignored files
# too, so deletion, not ignoring, is what keeps them out of snapshots.
firebase-debug.log
.firebase/
# Local source for the faces embedded into the artifact (AUD-08): the .woff2
# files plus fonts.json, read by scripts/gen-embedded-fonts.mjs at build time.
/fonts/
/Orga-naes.html.sha256
# Local rollback copies of the artifact kept while iterating: never ships. A
# tracked copy would be served as a second URL and silently stale the moment
# the artifact is rebuilt, so it stays here (and in snapshots, which mirror
# ignored files).
/Orga-naes.html.bak-*
/HANDOFF.md
/NEXT-PLAN.md
/PRODUCT.md
/REDESIGN-FINDINGS.md
/SECURITY.md
/PUBLISHING.md
/LOCAL-SETUP.md
/PF-DEBUG-LOGGER.md
/orga-naes-default-rtdb-export.json
